# -- Toilets taken from the building's own room records (2026-09-19, BUG-827) -------------------
# The toilet rows above put ONE toilet on every floor, in a room a generator chose -- a research
# laboratory, a plant room -- and a status was attached to each. "Where are the toilets on floor 2?"
# answered with floors 0, 1 and 3 and never mentioned floor 2, because that generated toilet was
# marked out of service and left out of the list.
#
# The building's OWN room list (bldg1_abacws_metadata.ttl) types eight rooms brick:Restroom, one
# male and one female on each of floors 2 to 5. Those are the toilets a person can walk to, so they
# are recorded here as amenities in their own right. NOT flagged simulated: the position is the
# building's own record, not a filled-in one. A floor answer prefers these to a generated row for
# the same floor. Floors 0 and 1 have no restroom room, so their generated rows stay -- the owner
# should confirm those two from the real plans.
#
# No lay term says male or female: "male toilets" is a substring of "female toilets", and a phrase
# match would have sent each question to the other room. The gender is in the label.

<http://abacwsbuilding.cardiff.ac.uk/abacws#Amenity_ToiletFacility_Room2_35>
    a ontosage:Amenity , ontosage:ToiletFacility ;
    rdfs:label "Toilet facility — Room 2.35 — Restroom (Male)"@en ;
    ontosage:layTerms "toilet, toilets, washroom, restroom, bathroom, wc" ;
    ontosage:locatedIn <http://abacwsbuilding.cardiff.ac.uk/abacws#Room2.35> ;
    ontosage:onFloor "Floor2" ;
    ontosage:locationText "Toilet facility in Room 2.35 — Restroom (Male) (floor 2)" ;
    ontosage:answerText "There is a toilet facility in Room 2.35 — Restroom (Male) on floor 2." .

<http://abacwsbuilding.cardiff.ac.uk/abacws#Amenity_ToiletFacility_Room2_36>
